{ The rook comes off the back rank, and Black keeps looking for counterplay. }
26. Bc4
{ The bishop takes the long diagonal, and a black pawn in front of the king is pinned — it cannot move. White mates the black king: the attack on the kingside never stopped, and that is what decided the game. }
